<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#A1.SS4" title="In Appendix A Appendix ‣ Self-Calibrated Consistency can Fight Back for Adversarial Robustness in Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">A.4 </span>Analysis of Robustness (under <math class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{a}=4/255" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>255</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{a}=4/255</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#A1.SS5" title="In Appendix A Appendix ‣ Self-Calibrated Consistency can Fight Back for Adversarial Robustness in Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">A.5 </span>Effects of Other Hyperparameters</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#A1.SS6" title="In Appendix A Appendix ‣ Self-Calibrated Consistency can Fight Back for Adversarial Robustness in Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">A.6 </span>Proof Sketch of Proposition (Hard-Negative Repulsion)</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#A1.SS7" title="In Appendix A Appendix ‣ Self-Calibrated Consistency can Fight Back for Adversarial Robustness in Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">A.7 </span>Proof Sketch of Proposition ( Suppression of spurious negatives)</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#A1.SS8" title="In Appendix A Appendix ‣ Self-Calibrated Consistency can Fight Back for Adversarial Robustness in Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">A.8 </span>The Use of Large Language Models</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
</ol></nav>
