<figure id="A1.T8" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 8: </span>
Classification accuracy (%) on clean images (Acc.) and adversarial images (Rob.) under 10-step PGD attack (<math id="A1.T8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{a}=4/255" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>255</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{a}=4/255</annotation></semantics></math>) across 16 datasets. The threat model assumes full access to model weights and gradients. We compare our paradigm against test-time defenses adapted from prior adversarial robustness studies, and include fine-tuned models as references. The last column shows the gains of SCC over the original CLIP.
</figcaption>
