</span></div>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F8" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.22785v1/Figure7.png" id="A1.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/162;" width="548" height="162" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 8: </span>
Effect of the warm-up step number <math id="A1.F8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> in short TTC: a moderate number yields the best robustness, while clean accuracy is unaffected. Effect of the Gaussian noise scale <math id="A1.F8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> (Sigma). Robustness improves with more views and larger <math id="A1.F8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, while clean accuracy drops.
</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.6 </span>Proof Sketch of Proposition (Hard-Negative Repulsion)</h3>

<div id="A1.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let
<math id="A1.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(\delta)\;=\;\cos\!\big(f_{\text{img}}(x+\delta),t_{\text{soft}}\big)-\max_{k\neq\hat{y}}\cos\!\big(f_{\text{img}}(x+\delta),t_{k}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.216em;" width="1.216em"><mi>cos</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>img</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>soft</mtext></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.216em;" width="1.216em"><mi>cos</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>img</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(\delta)\;=\;\cos\!\big(f_{\text{img}}(x+\delta),t_{\text{soft}}\big)-\max_{k\neq\hat{y}}\cos\!\big(f_{\text{img}}(x+\delta),t_{k}\big)</annotation></semantics></math>
and define <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{cm}(\delta)=m(\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{cm}(\delta)=m(\delta)</annotation></semantics></math>.
We analyze one PGD-ascent step</p>
<table id="A1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\delta^{+}\;=\;\Pi_{\|\cdot\|_{p}\leq\epsilon}\!\Big(\delta\;+\;\alpha\,\mathrm{sign}\!\big(\nabla_{\delta}\mathcal{L}_{cm}(\delta)\big)\Big),\qquad\alpha&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mi>α</mi><mpadded style="width:1.756em;" width="1.756em"><mi>sign</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>δ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{+}\;=\;\Pi_{\|\cdot\|_{p}\leq\epsilon}\!\Big(\delta\;+\;\alpha\,\mathrm{sign}\!\big(\nabla_{\delta}\mathcal{L}_{cm}(\delta)\big)\Big),\qquad\alpha&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumptions.</span> (i) In a small neighborhood of <math id="A1.SS6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, the maximizer in the second term is unique and fixed, i.e., there is an active index <math id="A1.SS6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j^{\star}(\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j^{\star}(\delta)</annotation></semantics></math> so the max is smooth; (ii) <math id="A1.SS6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{img}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>img</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{img}}</annotation></semantics></math> is differentiable and its Jacobian is bounded; (iii) either the projection is inactive (interior step) or its effect is <math id="A1.SS6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\alpha^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\alpha^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS6.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 1 (First–order increase).</span>
With the active competitor fixed, <math id="A1.SS6.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> is differentiable. By Taylor’s theorem,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(\delta^{+})\;=\;m(\delta)\;+\;\alpha\,\big\langle\nabla_{\delta}m(\delta),\,\mathrm{sign}\!\big(\nabla_{\delta}m(\delta)\big)\big\rangle\;+\;O(\alpha^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>δ</mi></msub><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.756em;" width="1.756em"><mi>sign</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>δ</mi></msub><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(\delta^{+})\;=\;m(\delta)\;+\;\alpha\,\big\langle\nabla_{\delta}m(\delta),\,\mathrm{sign}\!\big(\nabla_{\delta}m(\delta)\big)\big\rangle\;+\;O(\alpha^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A1.SS6.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle g,\mathrm{sign}(g)\rangle=\|g\|_{1}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>sign</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle g,\mathrm{sign}(g)\rangle=\|g\|_{1}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that</p>
<table id="A1.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(\delta^{+})\;\geq\;m(\delta)\;+\;\alpha\,\big\|\nabla_{\delta}m(\delta)\big\|_{1}\;+\;O(\alpha^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>δ</mi></msub><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(\delta^{+})\;\geq\;m(\delta)\;+\;\alpha\,\big\|\nabla_{\delta}m(\delta)\big\|_{1}\;+\;O(\alpha^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS6.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 2 (Relation to <math id="A1.SS6.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{cm}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{cm}</annotation></semantics></math>).</span>
By definition <math id="A1.SS6.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{cm}=m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{cm}=m</annotation></semantics></math>, hence the PGD-ascent direction aligns with <math id="A1.SS6.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\delta}m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>δ</mi></msub><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\delta}m</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, for sufficiently small <math id="A1.SS6.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(\delta^{+})\;\geq\;m(\delta)\;+\;O(\alpha^{2})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(\delta^{+})\;\geq\;m(\delta)\;+\;O(\alpha^{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.p4.2" class="ltx_p">i.e., the semantic margin is monotonically non-decreasing up to second-order terms.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS6.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 3 (Active-index changes &amp; projection).</span>
If the active negative <math id="A1.SS6.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j^{\star}(\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j^{\star}(\delta)</annotation></semantics></math> switches, <math id="A1.SS6.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> remains subdifferentiable; PGD uses a subgradient and the above inequality holds with <math id="A1.SS6.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\delta}m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>δ</mi></msub><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\delta}m</annotation></semantics></math> replaced by a subgradient. When projection onto the <math id="A1.SS6.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>-ball is active, the component removed is orthogonal to the feasible set’s tangent cone, contributing at most <math id="A1.SS6.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\alpha^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\alpha^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS6.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Conclusion.</span>
Under these mild regularity assumptions, one PGD-ascent step on <math id="A1.SS6.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{cm}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{cm}</annotation></semantics></math> increases the margin <math id="A1.SS6.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(x+\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(x+\delta)</annotation></semantics></math> monotonically up to <math id="A1.SS6.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\alpha^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\alpha^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. Iteration therefore <em id="A1.SS6.p6.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">repels the hard negative</em> and prevents drift toward confusable classes, which proves the proposition.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.7 </span>Proof Sketch of Proposition ( Suppression of spurious negatives)</h3>

<div id="A1.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{z}_{j}\triangleq\tfrac{1}{L}\sum_{i=1}^{L}z^{(i)}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>L</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{z}_{j}\triangleq\tfrac{1}{L}\sum_{i=1}^{L}z^{(i)}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> and let
<math id="A1.SS7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j^{\dagger}\in\arg\max_{j\neq y^{\star}}\bar{z}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j^{\dagger}\in\arg\max_{j\neq y^{\star}}\bar{z}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>
be an index achieving the maximum of the averaged logits (excluding <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>).
Then</p>
<table id="A1.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{j\neq y^{\star}}\bar{z}_{j}=\bar{z}_{j^{\dagger}}=\frac{1}{L}\sum_{i=1}^{L}z^{(i)}_{j^{\dagger}}\;\leq\;\frac{1}{L}\sum_{i=1}^{L}\max_{j\neq y^{\star}}z^{(i)}_{j}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>L</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>z</mi><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>L</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{j\neq y^{\star}}\bar{z}_{j}=\bar{z}_{j^{\dagger}}=\frac{1}{L}\sum_{i=1}^{L}z^{(i)}_{j^{\dagger}}\;\leq\;\frac{1}{L}\sum_{i=1}^{L}\max_{j\neq y^{\star}}z^{(i)}_{j},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS7.p1.2" class="ltx_p">since for each <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{(i)}_{j^{\dagger}}\leq\max_{j\neq y^{\star}}z^{(i)}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{(i)}_{j^{\dagger}}\leq\max_{j\neq y^{\star}}z^{(i)}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This proves
<math id="A1.SS7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{j\neq y^{\star}}\bar{z}_{j}\leq\tfrac{1}{L}\sum_{i=1}^{L}\max_{j\neq y^{\star}}z^{(i)}_{j}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>L</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{j\neq y^{\star}}\bar{z}_{j}\leq\tfrac{1}{L}\sum_{i=1}^{L}\max_{j\neq y^{\star}}z^{(i)}_{j}.</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<figure id="algorithm1" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span>SCC: Self-Calibrated Consistency</figcaption>
<div id="algorithm1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm1.4.1" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm1.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> </span>image <math id="algorithm1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, text embeddings <math id="algorithm1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{t_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{t_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, budget <math id="algorithm1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, steps <math id="algorithm1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, views <math id="algorithm1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>, temp <math id="algorithm1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.2.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm1.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> </span>predicted label <math id="algorithm1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.3" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">/* </span><span id="algorithm1.4.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Short warm-up (TTC) to stabilize predictions  */</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.4" class="ltx_listingline">Initialize <math id="algorithm1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\text{warm}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mtext>warm</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\text{warm}}=0</annotation></semantics></math>; run <math id="algorithm1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\text{warm}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mtext>warm</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\text{warm}}</annotation></semantics></math> PGD-ascent steps on TTC to obtain <math id="algorithm1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x+\delta_{\text{warm}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mtext>warm</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x+\delta_{\text{warm}}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.5" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">/* </span><span id="algorithm1.4.5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Multi-view pseudo-label on the warmed input  */</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.6" class="ltx_listingline">Sample <math id="algorithm1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> augmented views <math id="algorithm1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{v_{i}(x+\delta_{\text{warm}})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mtext>warm</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{v_{i}(x+\delta_{\text{warm}})\}</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.7" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{z}=\tfrac{1}{V}\sum_{i}f_{\text{img}}(v_{i}(x+\delta_{\text{warm}}))^{\top}[t_{k}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>V</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>img</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mtext>warm</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{z}=\tfrac{1}{V}\sum_{i}f_{\text{img}}(v_{i}(x+\delta_{\text{warm}}))^{\top}[t_{k}]</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.8" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=\mathrm{softmax}(\bar{z}/T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=\mathrm{softmax}(\bar{z}/T)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="algorithm1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}=\arg\max_{k}p_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}=\arg\max_{k}p_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="algorithm1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{soft}}=\sum_{k}p_{k}t_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>soft</mtext></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{soft}}=\sum_{k}p_{k}t_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.9" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">/* </span><span id="algorithm1.4.9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Counterattack optimization (sign-PGD ascent; shared <math id="algorithm1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>)  */</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.10" class="ltx_listingline">Initialize <math id="algorithm1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=0</annotation></semantics></math>;;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.11" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm1.4.11.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algorithm1.4.11.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_upright">to</span> <math id="algorithm1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm1.4.11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.12" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f=f_{\text{img}}(x+\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>img</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=f_{\text{img}}(x+\delta)</annotation></semantics></math>; 
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.13" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\text{cm}}=\langle f,t_{\text{soft}}\rangle-\max_{j\neq\hat{y}}\langle f,t_{j}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>cm</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>soft</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{cm}}=\langle f,t_{\text{soft}}\rangle-\max_{j\neq\hat{y}}\langle f,t_{j}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>; 
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.14" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\text{drift}}=\|f-f_{\text{img}}(x)\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>drift</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>img</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{drift}}=\|f-f_{\text{img}}(x)\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>; 
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.15" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\leftarrow\Pi_{\|\delta\|_{\infty}\leq\epsilon}\!\big(\delta+\alpha\,\mathrm{sign}(\nabla_{\delta}(\lambda_{cm}L_{\text{cm}}+L_{\text{drift}}))\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>sign</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>δ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>cm</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>drift</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\leftarrow\Pi_{\|\delta\|_{\infty}\leq\epsilon}\!\big(\delta+\alpha\,\mathrm{sign}(\nabla_{\delta}(\lambda_{cm}L_{\text{cm}}+L_{\text{drift}}))\big)</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.16" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\leftarrow\texttt{StepWeightedFuse}(\{\delta^{(s)}\}_{s=0}^{S};\,\tau,\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">StepWeightedFuse</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\leftarrow\texttt{StepWeightedFuse}(\{\delta^{(s)}\}_{s=0}^{S};\,\tau,\beta)</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.17" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.17.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">/* </span><span id="algorithm1.4.17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Final prediction (logit averaging on shared-<math id="algorithm1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> views)  */</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.18" class="ltx_listingline">Form views <math id="algorithm1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{v_{i}(x+\delta)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{v_{i}(x+\delta)\}</annotation></semantics></math>; ;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.19" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{z}=\tfrac{1}{V}\sum_{i}f_{\text{img}}(v_{i}(x+\delta))^{\top}[t_{k}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>V</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>img</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{z}=\tfrac{1}{V}\sum_{i}f_{\text{img}}(v_{i}(x+\delta))^{\top}[t_{k}]</annotation></semantics></math>; ;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.20" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}=\arg\max\mathrm{softmax}(\bar{z})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>softmax</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}=\arg\max\mathrm{softmax}(\bar{z})</annotation></semantics></math>.


</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.8 </span>The Use of Large Language Models</h3>

<div id="A1.SS8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Large language models were used to improve the clarity and presentation of writing.
All methodological design, experiments, and analysis were conducted by the authors.</p>
</div>
</section>
